From fefab95abf2b7b916fbaccb4410253ce2eb41515 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hiper25 <whydonit@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 05:03:40 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] media: meson-sc2: Honor explicit compressed OUTPUT capacities

SC2_SOURCE_SIZE is both the default compressed buffer capacity and the
minimum used by TRY_FMT. This rounds an explicit smaller userspace
capacity back to 8 MiB. Six HEVC source buffers then consume 48 MiB even
when userspace negotiated a sufficient smaller capacity.

Retain the 8 MiB default when sizeimage is unspecified. For explicit
capacities, retain the existing upper bound and use a 4 KiB lower bound.
The negotiated queue size, bytesused checks and private parser staging
bounds continue to define ownership and reject oversized submissions.

This does not change CAPTURE slots, DPB demand, CMA reservation, parser
staging allocation or codec/profile admission.

Change-Id: Ibf1adcfb48cd766427f6b42e9bb53c110baf69d1
---
 .../media/platform/amlogic/meson-sc2-vdec/meson_sc2_vdec.c  | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/amlogic/meson-sc2-vdec/meson_sc2_vdec.c b/drivers/media/platform/amlogic/meson-sc2-vdec/meson_sc2_vdec.c
index a81af5d469a6..d2504c06fc46 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/amlogic/meson-sc2-vdec/meson_sc2_vdec.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/amlogic/meson-sc2-vdec/meson_sc2_vdec.c
@@ -141,8 +141,10 @@ static int sc2_try_fmt(struct file *file, void *priv, struct v4l2_format *f)
 	pix->field = V4L2_FIELD_NONE;
 	pix->num_planes = 1;
 	memset(pix->plane_fmt, 0, sizeof(pix->plane_fmt));
-	pix->plane_fmt[0].sizeimage = clamp_t(u32, size, SC2_SOURCE_SIZE,
-					     32U * 1024U * 1024U);
+	/* The default is not a minimum for an explicit userspace capacity. */
+	pix->plane_fmt[0].sizeimage = size ?
+		clamp_t(u32, size, 4U * 1024U, 32U * 1024U * 1024U) :
+		SC2_SOURCE_SIZE;
 	if (!pix->colorspace)
 		pix->colorspace = V4L2_COLORSPACE_REC709;
 	memset(pix->reserved, 0, sizeof(pix->reserved));
